ana (docs): Quick sync — making a tiny doc entry: concise mitigations for 429s/timeouts when large contexts or cold KV cache are involved. Need two tiny SDK snippets, a short customer checklist, and a migration note. Who can review wording?

leo (eng-runtime): TL;DR: honor Retry-After if present; otherwise use exponential backoff + full jitter; pad retries to ~3 then failover to lighter model. Note: KV-cache cold starts can cause first-request timeouts — recommend a warmup or a single quick retry.

tara (devex): JS snippet (AbortController + retry):```js
async function callApiWithRetry(url, opts = {}, retries = 3) {
  for (let i = 0; i <= retries; i++) {
    const c = new AbortController();
    const t = setTimeout(() => c.abort(), opts.timeout || 60000);
    try {
      const r = await fetch(url, { ...opts, signal: c.signal });
      clearTimeout(t);
      if (r.status === 429) {
        const ra = r.headers.get('Retry-After');
        const wait = ra ? Number(ra) : Math.min(Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random(), 30);
        await new Promise(s => setTimeout(s, wait * 1000));
        continue;
      }
      if (!r.ok) throw new Error('http');
      return await r.json();
    } catch (e) {
      clearTimeout(t);
      if (e.name === 'AbortError' && i < retries) {
        await new Promise(s => setTimeout(s, (Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random()) * 1000));
        continue;
      }
      throw e;
    }
  }
}
```

